      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes the `SGLANG_USE_AITER=0` crash reported in #46628 (part 2). It does not address the GSM8K accuracy loss tracked in the same issue.\n\nLaunching `neuralmagic/Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct-v0.1-FP8` on ROCm with `SGLANG_USE_AITER=0` fails in the qkv projection:\n\nfp8_kernel.py:1030 native_static_quant_fp8: output.copy(output_data)\nRuntimeError: The size of tensor a (17) must match the size of tensor b (16) at non-singleton dimension 0\n\nOn ROCm without CUTLASS FP8, `apply_fp8_linear` pads activations to 17 rows for `torch._scaled_mm` (`fp8_utils.py`, `output_padding = 17`), so `scaled_fp8_quant` allocates `max(17, M)` output rows. The AITER kernel writes only the first `M` rows, but the native PyTorch fallback copied its `M`-row result into the whole padded tensor. Any batch under 17 tokens therefore crashes: CUDA graph capture at bs=16, or the first batches with `--disable-cuda-graph` (`17 vs 7`).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/kernels/ops/quantization/fp8_kernel.py`: `_native_static_quant_fp8` copies into `output[: input.shape[0]]` instead of `output`, matching what the AITER `static_per_tensor_quant` kernel writes. Padding rows stay uninitialized as before; the callers slice them away.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A. Behavior changes only where the old code raised. When `M >= 17`, or padding is off, `output[:M]` is the whole tensor and the result is identical. The AITER path is untouched.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A. Same computation, now written to a slice view.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). The function is only defined under `if _is_hip:`, so it can't be imported off ROCm. I reproduced both error messages from the issue (`17 vs 16`, `17 vs 7`) in plain PyTorch on CPU with the old copy, and confirmed the new copy succeeds for both shapes. Happy to add a HIP-only test if preferred.\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). No docs affected.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). N/A, see above.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\nI don't have AMD hardware, so I haven't run the end-to-end launch on MI300X. A check from someone with access, or AMD CI, would be appreciated.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40463286503](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40463286503)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40463286452](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40463286452)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40463286518](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40463286518)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
